content:
E33 confirms 406 pending messages with 0 attempts for orders created after t=590 — these have never been touched by the worker. The worker is running (E5 shows messages_processed at 8.00/s) and processing some messages, but 406 remain at 0 attempts. This is consistent with a simple backlog from the order burst (E6: peak 12.73/s at t=590) that the worker hasn't caught up to yet — the worker is draining the queue but hasn't reached these messages. The 174 invariant violations are the subset of those 406 that have been pending for more than 2 minutes. No new fault; the worker rollback fixed the root cause and the queue is actively draining. The repair is simply to requeue/surface the orphaned orders so the worker picks them up within the SLA window.

